{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/246439-hypothetical-guilds","id":246439,"title":"Hypothetical Guilds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-01T16:43:47-07:00","id":246439,"title":"Hypothetical Guilds","content":"According to <u>Guildhalls of the Deathless</u> (p.89), the five (six!) guilds have existed for centuries at the least, and a Deathless can't just start a guild on her own. That said, the <u>Demon</u> and <u>God-Machine</u> books have shown the possibilities of alternate timelines. In some of these alternate pasts/presents, who's to say what sort of Guilds may have formed?<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas on what these alterna-Guilds may be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T17:03:25-07:00","id":246460,"title":"","content":"Even Guildhalls mentions it may be possible to start a Guild, though it would be very difficult and take, at the least, several centuries to really establish. So who's to say there isn't some other Guild laying around even without the time-splinters?<br /> <br /> I imagine it'd be small and fairly localized but isolated. Perhaps that's why so many Arisen avoid Australia? But you'd also have to consider how they interact with relics, as relic-creation was the foundation of each Guild back in Irem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T08:05:10-07:00","id":246801,"title":"","content":"My Idea so far<br /> <br /> Explorer guild: (an offshot of the Maa-kep and Mesen-Nebu) ,their job is to make first contact with other cultures and to subtley learn more about non-Iremitic Magic and Relics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe also a Guild of the Web : a Post Irem Guild dedicated to gain control over Mass media and internet and reform Society to resemble more the Nameless Empire (via stuff like Irem Televangelism XD )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T13:09:57-07:00","id":247090,"title":"","content":"They're not guilds, technically, but I still recommend checking out my Sample Factions thread. It should be easy to convert my factions into guilds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T17:12:53-07:00","id":248259,"title":"","content":"OK, so we have our prospective Guilds; what would their Guild Affinities be like? I realize that Affinities can be too complex to just belt out, but what sort of themes would be covered by the Affinities of, say, the Explorer Guild, or a Guild dedicated to military matters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T05:30:56-07:00","id":248761,"title":"","content":"Well on the explorers i would say something about movement/travel and perception.<br /> A Militrary guild could have stuff like tactic ( maybe an affinity wich only works as a team) and intimidation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T12:22:11-07:00","id":249059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/246439-hypothetical-guilds?p=248761#post248761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Militrary guild could have stuff like tactic ( maybe an affinity wich only works as a team) and intimidation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually remember bringing that up at one point on this forum.<br /> <br /> The opinions ranged from &quot;They were taken down into Duat to conquer it&quot; to &quot;the existing guilds fill that roll already and just gathered the rabble to zerg the enemy&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:10:39-07:00","id":249267,"title":"","content":"The Military doesn't quite fit in with the rest of them, you have to admit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T16:21:42-07:00","id":249270,"title":"","content":"It's pretty firmly established in the books that Irem's military forces were slaves (the class below the guilds) led by nobles (the class above the guilds). Only the Maa-Kep Flail Bearers came close to the army, in that they were sometimes responsible for driving slave soldiers into battle. The Shemsu Temple Protectors of the Su-Menent also had a martial tradition, but they were still priests first.<br /> <br /> None of that prevents a new martial Guild being birthed in the manner described in Guildhalls. They just wouldn't have a legacy going back to Irem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T09:49:27-07:00","id":252432,"title":"","content":"Hmm. A Sibling/Offshoot/Sub-Guild of the Maa Kep would probably work best for a Military oriented group. Their 'middle management' outlook dovetails nicely into leading smaller units of the legions as subordinates of the Generals and other sundry higher-ups. And I can totally see their Amulets specialty fitting in with militaria (Iremite versions of dog tags, medals of merit, and what-all-else).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}